---
title: Vegan Butter Chicken
portions: 4
category: Curry
source: "https://connoisseurusveg.com/vegan-butter-chicken/"
---

## Cashew base

[Blend] Place the @cashews{110 g} and the @vegetable-stock{180 ml} in a #food processor{}. Blend to a smooth paste.

## Curry

[Sweat] Melt the @vegan-butter{28 g} in a large #skillet{} over medium heat. Add the @onion{150 g}(finely chopped) and sweat until soft and translucent, ~{5 min}.

[Brown] Add the @seitan{448 g}(torn into bite-sized pieces). Cook, stirring frequently, until it begins to brown, ~{5 min}.

[Bloom] Stir in the @garlic{9 g}(minced), the @ginger{8 g}(grated), the @garam-masala{7 g}, the @cumin{2 g} and the @paprika{2 g}. Cook until very fragrant, ~{1 min}.

[Simmer] Stir in the remaining @vegetable-stock{180 ml}, the @canned-tomatoes{400 g} and the @tomato-paste{17 g}. Bring to a boil, then lower the heat and simmer, stirring occasionally, ~{10 min}.

[Finish] Stir in the cashew paste and cook until the sauce comes back up to a simmer. Season with @salt{} and pepper to taste. Sprinkle with fresh @cilantro{}.

## Serve

[Serve] Serve over @basmati-rice{300 g}(cooked).
